<item><title>Cameroon opens Awae-Esse-Soa road serving 22 villages</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-opens-awae-esse-soa-road-serving-22-villages-343d8c/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-opens-awae-esse-soa-road-serving-22-villages-343d8c/</guid><category>Cameroon</category><description>The 82,252 km route links three communes to national roads and routes into the Central African Republic, with faster transport for farm produce.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 08:52:43 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" length="34085" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Cameroon funds 62.6% of public investment from domestic resources</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-funds-62-6-of-public-investment-from-domestic-52d8f3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-funds-62-6-of-public-investment-from-domestic-52d8f3/</guid><category>Cameroon</category><description>Finance Minister Louis Paul Motaze told lawmakers that domestic allocations rose by CFA261 billion in 2025 while external funding fell by CFA13.9 billion.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:40:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-funds-62-6-of-public-investment-from-domestic-52d8f3/share.jpg" length="44450" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-funds-62-6-of-public-investment-from-domestic-52d8f3/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Cameroon signs coffee pact opening African body to consuming countries</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-signs-coffee-pact-opening-african-body-to-06cb40/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-signs-coffee-pact-opening-african-body-to-06cb40/</guid><category>Cameroon</category><description>The agreement gives coffee-producing and consuming governments a forum to discuss processing, marketing and sales within Africa.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:28:45 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" length="34085" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Institutional investors hold 38.3% of Cameroon’s Treasury bonds</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/institutional-investors-hold-38-3-of-cameroon-s-treasury-c402f3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/institutional-investors-hold-38-3-of-cameroon-s-treasury-c402f3/</guid><category>Cameroon</category><description>Their bond holdings fell by CFA19.23 billion in October, while Treasury bill holdings rose 33.6% to CFA68.89 billion.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 08:34:54 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/institutional-investors-hold-38-3-of-cameroon-s-treasury-c402f3/share.jpg" length="42969" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/institutional-investors-hold-38-3-of-cameroon-s-treasury-c402f3/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
